# Arabic RTL UI

- Preserve Arabic RTL behavior in both pages. Check `dir="rtl"` assumptions before changing layout or DOM order.
- Keep shared visual behavior centralized in `assets/css/styles.css`; avoid inline styling unless already local to a tiny dynamic fragment.
- Prefer `textContent` for dynamic Arabic copy. Use `innerHTML` only for trusted local markup that needs line breaks or structure.
- Test responsive table/card behavior on `index.html` and `person.html` after layout changes.
- Use readable Arabic typography and generous line height for verse snippets, ranges, and completion labels.
- Keep person colors and day status colors consistent across full schedule and personal view.
